{
  "title": "ramekin-core: dedupe the two near-parallel ~245-line blog \
extraction functions",
  "description": "src/extract/blog.rs:198-440 \
(extract_recipe_from_unstructured_blog, ~243 lines) and :472-720 \
(extract_recipe_from_virtualweberbullet, ~248 lines) are both single \
monolithic functions implementing the same 'walk paragraphs -> detect section \
headers -> collect ingredient/instruction lines' strategy — one generic, one \
hardcoded to a single domain (virtualweberbullet.com).\n\
\n\
Fix: extract the shared chunk-walking / section-detection / ingredient-line \
collection into helpers (some already exist: looks_like_ingredient_list, \
extract_ingredient_lines_from_chunk) and have the site-specific function reuse \
them, isolating the one-off domain special-case to its actual deltas.\n\
\n\
Intended to be behavior-preserving, but this is extraction code: rerun `make \
pipeline` and commit any data/ diffs — if diffs appear, inspect them; \
unintended ones mean the refactor changed behavior.",
